    summary_60s: 'The Oyo Empire traced its origin to Ile-Ife , the spiritual home of the Yoruba people. It was founded by Oranmiyan , a descendant of Oduduwa. By the late 15th century , the Oyo Empire had expanded its influence across much of Yorubaland , becoming a dominant political and militar',
